Fillets: a rounding rolling on an edge from one OnSame end of the spine to
the other, whose walk past an end stopped on the seam of the other face
before the ball comes tangent to the edge's face (mitcad#236, with 0340).

The case of 0340 (a rod with a ridge, the ridge's end rounded wider than
the lens it ends with), where the rod's seam runs past the spine's end
between the lens's tip and the point where the ball comes tangent to the
ridge's side: the walk past that end stopped on the seam, a blend rolling
on an edge ends at the spine's end there (0011), and the corner had no
point where 0340's cut by the ridge's side starts.

- ChFi3d_Builder::RolledEndToEndAcrossSeam, called by PerformSetOfSurf: a
  stripe of one SurfData rolling on an edge Er of its face B, Er running
  from the spine's first vertex to its last, both ends OnSame, where at an
  end the contact on the other face N stopped on N's seam short of the
  ball's tangency to B: the blend is walked again from the middle of the
  SurfData, both ways, N's surface unbounded, still rolling on Er, and
  replaces the SurfData when both its ends are such tangencies. Its curve
  on N is taken in the period of the old one at the start; its parts
  across N's seam lie past the faces at the ends, which cut them off.

Upstream: new.
